WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.051
Press the shortcut on any page to select a region.

2
00:00:07.151 --> 00:00:11.018
Drag across the links you want. Each match lights up.

3
00:00:11.118 --> 00:00:13.637
7 links selected, and the card says where they’ll go.

4
00:00:13.737 --> 00:00:16.309
Add them to a collection, or copy two columns right away.

5
00:00:16.709 --> 00:00:20.394
Anchor text, URL and source page stay in separate fields.

6
00:00:20.494 --> 00:00:24.881
An image link keeps empty anchor text. Its alt text is kept as a separate label.

7
00:00:24.981 --> 00:00:31.154
Group by URL when you want. Every label stays visible.

8
00:00:31.254 --> 00:00:38.865
Open a group to see each occurrence and where it came from.

9
00:00:38.965 --> 00:00:42.938
Switch back any time. All 7 occurrences are still there.

10
00:00:43.038 --> 00:00:45.342
Download Excel, CSV, JSON, BibTeX and more.

11
00:00:45.742 --> 00:00:48.242
Two clean columns: anchor text and URL.

12
00:00:48.342 --> 00:00:51.142
The image link’s anchor text stays empty. Nothing is invented.

13
00:00:51.542 --> 00:00:55.470
New in 1.0: on a PDF’s tab, Link Meteor reads the links inside the PDF.

14
00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:59.965
A preview shows every link with its page. Nothing is saved yet.

15
00:01:00.065 --> 00:01:05.259
Add them in one step, with the PDF itself as a link.
